+# HIL Scenario Runbook — Gazebo / Isaac Sim
+
+Purpose
+- Provide a repeatable Hardware-In-The-Loop (HIL) scenario to validate agent→ROS2→robot control loops in simulation before any physical deployment.
+
+Prerequisites
+- Gazebo (or Isaac Sim) installed on test host.
+- Aegis ROS2 adapter image deployed and able to communicate with simulation topics.
+- Validator service (enhanced_validator) available to consume telemetry and assert safety properties.
+
+Scenario: simple navigation + obstacle avoidance
+1) Start simulation
+   - Launch Gazebo world: gazebo --verbose worlds/arena.world
+   - Ensure robot model (URDF) is spawned and exposes /cmd_vel and /scan topics.
+2) Deploy ROS2 adapter
+   - docker run --rm --network host <registry>/aegis-ros2-adapter:latest
+3) Start agent in staging to issue a "navigate" plan
+   - Agent issues command to /aegis/commands: {"action":"move","params":{"x":5,"y":0,"speed":0.5}}
+4) Monitor safety
+   - The ROS2 adapter should reject geofence-exceeding commands.
+   - The simulation LIDAR (/scan) should detect obstacles; agent planner should adapt.
+5) Fault injection
+   - Simulate actuator delay or sensor dropout and verify remediation workflow triggers (Argo) and records evidence.
+6) Post-run validation
