+# Safety & Certification Checklist — Robotics / Drones / Vehicles
+
+This checklist maps typical engineering tasks and evidence required to approach certification and safe operation in physical domains.
+
+1) System & Architecture
+ - Define operational domain, use-cases, and environment assumptions (ODD).
+ - Identify safety-critical components and single points of failure.
+ - Produce architecture diagram showing agent -> control -> hardware path with trust boundaries.
+
+2) Attestation & Identity
+ - Require hardware attestation (TPM/SGX/Nitro) for any controller that issues actuation commands.
+ - Document attestation flows, certificates, issuance policies and rotation schedules.
+ - Evidence: attestation logs, Vault PKI configs, Rekor indices for issued certs.
+
+3) Control Safety & Interlocks
+ - Implement hardware E-STOP, watchdog timers, and motion limits at the controller level.
+ - Ensure adapter enforces geofencing and velocity limits.
+ - Evidence: hardware test results, E-STOP activation logs, bench tests.
+
+4) HIL & Simulation
+ - Develop repeatable HIL scenarios (Gazebo/Isaac) that cover nominal, edge and failure modes.
+ - Automate HIL runs in CI and record telemetry for validators.
+ - Evidence: HIL run logs, validator reports, artifact bundles.
+
+5) Software Safety & Validation
+ - Unit tests, integration tests, and property-based tests for control loops.
+ - Model safety checks (hallucination detectors, RAG verification) before actions.
+ - Use OPA policies as policy-as-code for action approvals.
+ - Evidence: test matrices, coverage reports, OPA policy commit history.
+
+6) Human-in-the-loop & Overrides
+ - Define human roles and emergency procedures; implement multi-party overrides for critical actions.
+ - Evidence: audit trails of overrides, signing of override approvals (signed logs).
+
+7) Performance & Reliability
+ - Establish latency, jitter and SLO requirements for real-time control.
+ - Validate edge inference latency and failover procedures.
+ - Evidence: benchmark reports, stress test artifacts.
+
+8) Security & Supply-chain
+ - Enforce cosign + Rekor for all artifacts and tools; hardened builder provenance for any code that can actuate.
+ - SBOM for runtime images and tool containers; vulnerability mitigation records.
+ - Evidence: SBOMs, grype reports, cosign/Rekor entries.
+
+9) Regulatory & Standards
+ - Identify applicable standards (ISO 13482, ISO 26262, RTCA DO-178C, etc.) and map controls to them.
+ - Prepare required documentation: SRS, HARA (Hazard Analysis and Risk Assessment), safety case.
+ - Evidence: completed SRS, HARA, safety case documents.
+
+10) Audit & Certification
+ - Package evidence bundles with signed provenance for external auditors.
+ - Track auditor findings, remediation plans, and closure evidence.
+ - Evidence: signed auditor report, re-submitted bundles, verification traces.
+
+Notes
+- Certification paths depend heavily on the physical domain and intended level of autonomy. Engage with domain experts early.
+- This checklist is a minimal, high-level starter — adapt and expand per domain/regulation.
+
